/**
 * @page TransferGuide Transfer and Further Development Guide
 *
 * @brief Technical documentation for rebuilding and extending the
 * rainwater monitoring prototype.
 *
 * This document describes all steps required to rebuild, deploy,
 * maintain and further develop the rainwater monitoring system.
 *
 *
 * @section SystemOverview System Overview
 *
 * The prototype consists of the following components:
 *
 * - HAN IoT Node
 * - LoRaWAN network (The Things Stack)
 * - Node-RED integration
 * - MariaDB database
 * - Grafana dashboard
 *
 * Sensor data is collected by the LoRaWAN node, transmitted through
 * The Things Stack, processed by Node-RED and stored in a MariaDB
 * database. Grafana is used to visualize the collected data.
 *
 *
 * @section RepositoryStructure Repository Structure
 *
 * The project consists of the following repositories:
 *
 * - LoRaWAN Node Application
 * - Payload Encoder / Decoder
 * - Database Scripts
 * - Node-RED Flows
 * - Grafana Dashboard Configuration
 *
 *
 * @section HardwareSetup Hardware Setup
 *
 * Required hardware:
 *
 * - HAN IoT Node shield
 * - LoRaWAN gateway
 * - USB programming cable
 *
 * Prototype sensor mapping:
 *
 * - Red push button     -> Flow meter
 * - White potentiometer -> Water level sensor
 * - Red potentiometer   -> Battery voltage sensor
 *
 *
 * @section SoftwareSetup Software Setup
 *
 * Required software:
 *
 * - Arduino IDE
 * - HAN IoT Node libraries
 * - The Things Stack account
 * - Node-RED
 * - MariaDB
 * - Grafana
 *
 *
 * @section LoRaWANNodeSetup LoRaWAN Node Setup
 *
 * 1. Open the LoRaWAN node project in Arduino IDE.
 * 2. Configure OTAA credentials in:
 *
 * @code
 * ThingsNetworkConfig.h
 * @endcode
 *
 * 3. Compile the project.
 * 4. Upload the firmware to the HAN IoT Node.
 * 5. Verify successful OTAA join through the serial monitor.
 *
 *
 * @section PayloadFormat Payload Format
 *
 * The payload format is shared by the encoder, decoder and
 * TTN payload formatter.
 *
 * @verbatim
 *
 * +------------+-------------+------------------+
 * | Flow Meter | Level Meter | Battery Voltage  |
 * +------------+-------------+------------------+
 * | 1 byte     | 2 bytes     | 4 bytes          |
 * +------------+-------------+------------------+
 *
 * @endverbatim
 *
 * Total payload size:
 *
 * @code
 * 7 bytes
 * @endcode
 *
 *
 * @section TTNConfiguration The Things Stack Configuration
 *
 * 1. Create an application.
 * 2. Register the end device.
 * 3. Configure OTAA activation.
 * 4. Configure the JavaScript payload formatter.
 * 5. Enable MQTT integration.
 * 6. Verify successful uplink reception.
 *
 *
 * @section NodeREDSetup Node-RED Configuration
 *
 * The Node-RED flow consists of:
 *
 * - TTN MQTT input
 * - TTN message unifier
 * - Payload pre-processing
 * - Database insertion
 * - Dashboard and visualization integrations
 *
 * The pre-processing function performs:
 *
 * - Payload extraction
 * - Timestamp generation
 * - Device identification
 * - Gateway metadata extraction
 *
 *
 * @section DatabaseSetup Database Setup
 *
 * Create the database:
 *
 * @code
 * raintankNetwork
 * @endcode
 *
 * Execute:
 *
 * @code
 * raintankNetwork.sql
 * @endcode
 *
 * to create all required tables.
 *
 * Tables:
 *
 * - device
 * - measurement
 * - radio_metadata
 *
 *
 * @section GrafanaSetup Grafana Configuration
 *
 * 1. Create a MariaDB data source.
 * 2. Connect to database:
 *
 * @code
 * raintankNetwork
 * @endcode
 *
 * 3. Create dashboards for:
 *
 * - Water level
 * - Water consumption
 * - Battery voltage
 * - RSSI
 * - SNR
 *
 * Use the measurement timestamp:
 *
 * @code
 * uplink_at
 * @endcode
 *
 * as the Grafana time field.
 *
 *
 * @section Verification Verification Procedure
 *
 * Verify system operation using the following procedure:
 *
 * 1. Power the node.
 * 2. Verify OTAA join.
 * 3. Modify potentiometer values.
 * 4. Press the flow meter button.
 * 5. Verify uplinks in TTN.
 * 6. Verify database records.
 * 7. Verify Grafana visualizations.
 *
 *
 * @section FutureDevelopment Future Development
 *
 * Future improvements may be implemented in the following areas:
 *
 * Hardware:
 * - Physical water level sensor
 * - Physical flow sensor
 * - Temperature sensor
 * - Battery powered deployment
 *
 * LoRaWAN:
 * - Downlink support
 * - Remote configuration
 *
 * Software:
 * - Additional payload fields
 * - Alarm generation
 * - Historical reporting
 *
 * Database:
 * - Device management
 * - Gateway management
 * - Statistical analysis
 *
 * Dashboard:
 * - Consumption reports
 * - Monthly statistics
 * - Predictive maintenance indicators
 *
 *
 * @section Troubleshooting Troubleshooting
 *
 * No TTN uplinks:
 * - Verify OTAA credentials.
 * - Verify gateway coverage.
 *
 * No database records:
 * - Verify MQTT connection.
 * - Verify Node-RED flow status.
 * - Verify database credentials.
 *
 * No Grafana data:
 * - Verify MariaDB datasource configuration.
 * - Verify SQL queries.
 * - Verify timestamp field selection.
 *
 *
 * @section References References
 *
 * See also:
 * - @ref UseCase
 * - @ref ShieldLayout
 * - @ref ApplicationArchitecture
 * - @ref PayloadCodec
 * - @ref DatabaseDesign
 */